  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by reason of the size and internal dimensions of the proposed garage units and the access layout, would fail to provide functional and fit-for-purpose parking accommodation for modern sized vehicles. The garages would provide insufficient space for the safe and convenient manoeuvring of vehicles and for occupants to enter and exit parked vehicles, resulting in substandard parking facilities that would not adequately meet user requirements.. As such, the proposal is contrary to Policies D4, D3, H1 and H2 of the London Plan (2021), Policy CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy, and the National Planning Policy Framework",
    "The proposed development, by reason of the proposed use of the site as a commercial car park, represents an unacceptable change of use and inefficient use of a previously developed site within an urban location. The site has the potential to make a significantly greater contribution towards meeting identified housing needs within the brough and supporting the efficient use of land. As such, the proposal fails to optimise the development potential of the site and would prejudice the delivery of residential development. The proposal is therefore contrary to the objectives of sustainable development, urban regeneration and the effective use of land as set out in the National Planning Policy Framework and Policies H1 and H2 of the Development Plan, Policy CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy. k.",
    "The proposed development in the absence of an adequate Flood Risk Assessment and Sustainable Drainage Strategy, has failed to demonstrate that the proposed development would adequately manage surface water runoff, reduce flood risk, or incorporate appropriate SuDs systems in accordance with the London Plan drainage hierarchy and SuDS management principles. Furthermore, insufficient information has been provided regarding the existing and proposed drainage arrangements, the site's relationship with the adjoining Salmons Brook watercourse, compliance with the required river buffer zone, and measures to protect and enhance the water environment. As a result, the Local Planning Authority cannot be satisfied that the development would not increase flood risk either on-site or elsewhere, would safeguard the integrity of the adjoining watercourse The proposal is therefore contrary to Policies SI12 and SI13 of the London Plan (2021), Policy CP28 of the Enfield Core Strategy, Policies DMD 61, DMD 62 and DMD 63 of the Enfield Development Management Document, National Planning Policy Framework."
  ],
